      "text": "To find the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) for the equation \\[\n\\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right)^2 + \\left(\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4}\\right) = 12,\n\\] we start by letting \\( y = \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} \\). Then the equation becomes:\n\\[\ny^2 + y = 12.\n\\]\nRearrange this into a standard quadratic equation form:\n\\[\ny^2 + y - 12 = 0.\n\\]\nWe solve this quadratic equation using the quadratic formula \\( y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a} \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 1 \\), and \\( c = -12 \\):\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1^2 - 4 \\cdot 1 \\cdot (-12)}}{2 \\cdot 1} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{1 + 48}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{49}}{2} = \\frac{-1 \\pm 7}{2}.\n\\]\nThis gives us two solutions for \\( y \\):\n\\[\ny = \\frac{-1 + 7}{2} = 3 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad y = \\frac{-1 - 7}{2} = -4.\n\\]\nThus, we have two cases to consider:\n1. \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3 \\)\n2. \\( \\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4 \\)\n\n**Case 1:**\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = 3.\n\\]\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\\[\n4x-16 = 3(3x-4).\n\\]\nDistribute the 3 on the right side:\n\\[\n4x-16 = 9x-12.\n\\]\nRearrange to isolate \\( x \\):\n\\[\n-16 + 12 = 9x - 4x.\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n-4 = 5x \\implies x = -\\frac{4}{5}.\n\\]\n\n**Case 2:**\n\\[\n\\frac{4x-16}{3x-4} = -4.\n\\]\nMultiply both sides by \\( 3x-4 \\):\n\\[\n4x-16 = -4(3x-4).\n\\]\nDistribute the -4 on the right side:\n\\[\n4x-16 = -12x + 16.\n\\]\nRearrange to isolate \\( x \\):\n\\[\n4x + 12x = 16 + 16.\n\\]\nSimplify:\n\\[\n16x = 32 \\implies x = 2.\n\\]\n\nWe have two potential values for \\( x \\): \\( x = -\\frac{4}{5} \\) and \\( x = 2 \\). To determine which value is the greatest, we compare the two. Clearly, \\( 2 \\) is greater than \\( -\\frac{4}{5} \\).\n\nThus, the greatest possible value of \\( x \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{2}\n\\]",
